<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB's Gehrig says Swiss franc still seen as firm.</title>
<headline>SNB's Gehrig says Swiss franc still seen as firm.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bruno Gehrig, member of the Swiss National Bank's board, said the central bank still viewed the Swiss franc as firm, despite its recent weakening.</p>
<p>Gehrig also said in a speech the scope for higher inflation was slight due to the weak Swiss economy and unused production and employment potentials.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite the weakening, the franc must, now as before, be considered firm,&quot; Gehrig told a news conference, adding:</p>
<p>&quot;The scope for generally higher wages and prices remain slight for the foreseable future.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
